## THE REVISION TRAP
Treasury Bulletins publish preliminary (P) data updated in subsequent months as revised (R).
1. Check the month requested.
2. Search bulletins from 3-6 months AFTER the target date for revisions.
3. Prioritize figures marked (R) or found in the most recent publication.

## DATA EXTRACTION
- Scan for footnotes (*, 1/, 2/) — they contain unit multipliers and essential offsets.
- Verify the column header matches the EXACT category requested.
- Fiscal year ends June 30 (pre-1976) or September 30 (post-1976). Calendar year ends December 31.
- "Public debt" ≠ "total gross federal debt." "Saving notes" ≠ "savings bonds." "Series E" ≠ "Series EE."
- If the question says "total" and you found a line item, look for a parent row.
- "Budget Expenditures" (1940s) = "Outlays" (modern). Terminology evolves across decades.

